# gitmap allowlist — synthetic test fixtures ONLY.
#
# Every entry below was opened and read before being listed. A secret scanner is only worth having if a
# suppression costs more effort than fixing the finding, so each line records WHY the match is not a
# credential. Never add an entry to make a commit go through.
#
# Format: <detector-id>:<path>[:<fingerprint>]

# Placeholder API keys in a transcript-fetch test. Both are literal alphabet sequences
# (ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789) appended to a real-looking prefix, which is exactly what a
# synthetic fixture looks like and exactly what a real key does not.
openai-key:app/native/CodexLocalRetrieval.Native.Tests/TranscriptFetchTests.cs:be8381ecf7f2
github-token:app/native/CodexLocalRetrieval.Native.Tests/TranscriptFetchTests.cs:65c3ebbc31c6

# The same test asserts the built command carries an Authorization header; the token is the synthetic
# "bridge-token-abcdefgh12345678". The assertion is the point — it proves the header is constructed.
authorization-literal:app/native/CodexLocalRetrieval.Native.Tests/TranscriptFetchTests.cs:464c953fdc85

# NEGATIVE assertion, not a secret. retention.test.js:456 iterates a list of forbidden substrings (key and
# secret field names, a PEM armour header, and the host token) and asserts the journal contains NONE of them.
# The scanner matched the needle that this test exists to prove is absent. Deliberately NOT quoting the list
# here: an earlier version of this comment reproduced it verbatim and tripped the same detector on this file.
private-key-block:relay/tests/retention.test.js:b846fdb2d23a

# 79-byte fixture whose content begins "FIXTUR...". Consumed by relay/tests/backup-state.test.js, whose
# SECRETS list drives a test that secret-bearing files are NOT captured into backups. A real credential
# here would defeat the test's own purpose.
credential-file-path:relay/tests/fixtures/backup-state/local-control.cred

# Telemetry redaction fixtures. The literal is self-labelled FAKEexampleKEYnotreal0000000 and exists
# ONLY as the input to tests asserting that a secret inside an exception message is redacted BEFORE
# it reaches the durable event ledger — the exact accident that once burned a live key. Read all
# three call sites (lines 54, 93, 112) before trusting this entry.
openai-key:app/native/CodexLocalRetrieval.Native.Tests/SessionEventLedgerTests.cs:1aac09f88b8f
